  "text": "This work looks at a frequent pattern in a certain language’s sentences that I prefer to call an abbreviation rather than a deletion. Although others may have noticed it, no one has yet gathered many examples and shown that they all follow the same simple rule. By understanding what really happens, we can describe the process with a single, clear principle that covers a wide range of cases. The main benefit of this view is that it removes the need for complicated meaning‑based explanations of the resulting ambiguity. In my analysis, the two different readings come from two separate structures that exist before the abbreviation rule is applied, so the ambiguity is explained directly without invoking extra abstract forms or questionable transformations. Several concrete instances are then examined to illustrate the idea."
